  m_Name: Scene11_Context
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.SceneAgentContext
  sceneId: Scene11
  sceneTitle: Turn Data into a Graph
  askWattsonEnabled: 1
  covered:
  - "Everything from Scenes 5 to 10: voltage (V, volt), current (I, ampere), the
    circuit, the five readings (1 V \u2192 0.2 A ... 5 V \u2192 1.0 A), current rises
    with potential difference, doubling V doubles I."
  - Plotted with current I on the horizontal axis and potential difference V on the
    vertical axis, the five points lie on a straight line through the origin.
  - "For the nichrome wire at constant temperature, the potential difference across
    it is directly proportional to the current through it: V \u221D I."
  doNotSpoil:
  - Resistance
  - V / I = constant
  - The slope of the graph is the resistance
  - Ohms
  - V = IR
  - The name 'Ohm's law'
  - The Christmas-lights answer
  faq: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4466b06e54a5190418115a5ecb1b34d5, type: 2}
